# Team Mantis — Git Workflow

Project: Space Invaders (Java) — **Records & Achievements System**

---

## 1. Selected Git Workflow and Rationale

**Workflow: GitHub Flow**

GitHub Flow uses one long-lived branch (`main`) that is always stable and runnable. All work happens in short-lived branches that are merged back into `main` through pull requests.

**Why it fits our project**

- **Simple for a 9-person team.** There is only one permanent branch, so nobody has to track `develop`, `release`, or `hotfix` branches.
- **Small, focused features.** Our subsystem (records, achievements, related UI) splits naturally into small tasks that fit short-lived branches.
- **No versioned releases.** We integrate continuously into the course repository instead of shipping numbered versions, so Git Flow's release branches would be unnecessary overhead.
- **Other teams depend on us.** Keeping `main` always working means dependent teams can pull our latest code at any time without breaking their build.
- **Review built in.** Every change goes through a pull request, so every line of code is seen by at least one other member.

