## 6. Overall Development Workflow

### Steps

1. **Pick a task** — take or create an issue and assign yourself.
2. **Update `main`** — `git switch main` → `git pull origin main`.
3. **Create a branch** — `git switch -c feature/<description>`.
4. **Develop** — write code and commit in small, logical commits (Section 3).
5. **Sync** — rebase onto the latest `main` and resolve conflicts (Section 5).
6. **Push** — `git push -u origin feature/<description>`.
7. **Open a PR** — fill in the PR contents (Section 4).
8. **Review** — at least 1 teammate reviews; the author addresses feedback with new commits.
9. **Merge** — after approval, the author uses **Squash and merge**.
10. **Clean up** — delete the remote and local branch, then pull `main`.

### Diagram

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Pick or create an issue] --> B[Pull latest main]
    B --> C[Create branch<br/>feature/ · fix/ · refactor/ · docs/]
    C --> D[Write code &<br/>make small commits]
    D --> E[Rebase onto latest main]
    E --> F{Conflicts?}
    F -- Yes --> G[Author resolves,<br/>builds & tests]
    G --> H
    F -- No --> H[Push branch]
    H --> I[Open Pull Request]
    I --> J{Review:<br/>1 approval + build passes?}
    J -- Changes requested --> K[Address feedback<br/>push new commits]
    K --> J
    J -- Approved --> L[Squash and merge into main]
    L --> M[Delete branch]
    M --> B
```

